From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Melser <anton.melser@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:42:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] main-loop-unroll: let the host drive PostgresMain's loop

Under __PGLITE__ the host drives the backend one message exchange at a
time instead of PostgresMain looping on a socket:

- The body of PostgresMain's message loop moves into
  PostgresMainLoopOnce(), its ReadyForQuery step into
  PostgresSendReadyForQueryIfNecessary() and its sigsetjmp error
  recovery into PostgresMainLongJmp(); PostgresMain calls them. The
  moved code is re-indented, so the diff reads as a rewrite of the
  function rather than a move.
- postgresmain_sigjmp_buf, ignore_till_sync and send_ready_for_query
  are defined by the host code (pglite/src/pglitec/pglitec.c in the
  overlay), so their state survives between calls.
- Entry points for the host: pgl_startPGlite() (a dummy Port on a
  loopback address, the HBA load and the postmaster-environment flags),
  pgl_sendConnData() (AuthenticationOk, parameter status,
  BackendKeyData and ReadyForQuery), pgl_pq_flush() and
  pgl_getMyProcPort().
- While PGlite is active, a Terminate message keeps the runtime alive
  (pgl_setPGliteExitStatus(PGLITE_EXIT_ALIVE) and
  emscripten_exit_with_live_runtime()) instead of calling proc_exit(0).

Derived from electric-sql/postgres-pglite b133782cd759f08b3aeb263b80a963b39c7b7af1 (PostgreSQL 18.3 fork, PostgreSQL License)
---
 src/backend/tcop/postgres.c | 1357 ++++++++++++++++++++---------------
 1 file changed, 795 insertions(+), 562 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/backend/tcop/postgres.c b/src/backend/tcop/postgres.c
